A||N||1||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||2.5 Duke - Airbox modifications?||||5||
Z||000000||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||02-06-2001||01:23 AM||||I have read about a few modifications to the 2.5 L 4cylinder "Iron Duke" engine's intake system.<P>The engine has deburred intake and exhaust passages, an MSD 6-AL ignition, recent head gasket (including TBI, EGR, intake and exhaust manifold gaskets), Accel coil, new spark plug wires, Autolite plugs, vacuum hoses, thermostat housing and thermostat, new alternator, battery, starter, belts, radiator hoses, cap and rotor, ignition module, pickup coil, MAP sensor, TPS sensor, Filters (transmission, crankcase, air, and fuel), fuel pump, PCV valve, torque strut, etc.<P>After all of this I am having trouble believing a 1984 2.5L only made 92HP.  <P>My next steps are monolithic catalytic converter and an MSD adjustable timing control.  <P>I have to replace a damaged driver's side quarter panel.  I have a new panel.  I will reveal the airbox when I replace the old one.  So what's the best way to modify the air box for more flow?  <p>[This message has been edited by LuckyTheyWereEverMade (edited 02-06-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||02-06-2001||01:43 AM||||Pull out the air box and weigh down some trash can with it. Replace it with a 3' pipe you can find at Home Depot or other hardware store. Great sounds!||||reg||6
